+# Task 3 owned-browser implementation report
+
+## Scope and status
+Implemented only new OwnedBrowser Core/test paths and the exact owned-browser subplan/report. Base c769b53bb084b0109f023f7b5f64bea7d38d3060, branch aside/owned-browser-20261028. No shared project references or existing code changed. No UI, WebView2 host, extension, shell, account reads, browser launch, live settings or root-checkout writes. Existing CreateBrowserSession remains unchanged.
+
+## Exact public contract
+Namespace `OpenClicky.Core.OwnedBrowser`:
+```csharp
+public enum ProfileRemoval { Keep, Delete }
+public sealed record OwnedTab(Guid Id, string Url);
+public sealed record OwnedWorkspace(string Id, string Name, IReadOnlyList<OwnedTab> Tabs);
+public static class OwnedBrowserPolicy {
+    public const int MaxWorkspaces = 16, MaxTabsPerWorkspace = 32,
+        MaxTotalTabs = 128, MaxStateBytes = 1048576;
+    public static bool AllowsHostObjects { get; }
+    public static bool AllowsWebMessages { get; }
+    public static bool AllowsDownloads { get; }
+    public static bool AllowsExternalLaunch { get; }
+    public static bool AllowsPermission(string permission);
+    public static string CanonicalWorkspaceId(string id);
+    public static string AdmitNavigation(string url);
+}
+public sealed class OwnedBrowserStore : IDisposable {
+    public OwnedBrowserStore(string storageParent);
+    public IReadOnlyList<OwnedWorkspace> List();
+    public OwnedWorkspace CreateWorkspace(string id, string name);
+    public string GetProfileDirectory(string workspaceId);
+    public OwnedTab OpenTab(string workspaceId, string url);
+    public OwnedTab Navigate(string workspaceId, Guid tabId, string url);
+    public void CloseTab(string workspaceId, Guid tabId);
+    public void RemoveWorkspace(string workspaceId, ProfileRemoval profileRemoval);
+    public void Dispose();
+}
+```
+All policy booleans and permission requests deny. Profiles derive only from nonempty GUID N/D identities, canonicalized to lowercase N, under `storageParent/OwnedBrowser-v1/profiles/{id}`. No external profile input/import exists. Names limited to 100 characters; URLs to 4096. Snapshot collections are read-only. Default JSON is PascalCase, version 1; unknown/duplicate fields, invalid identities/URLs, duplicate tab IDs, excess caps, missing/null/oversized/corrupt state fail closed. No automatic recovery/reset.
+
+## Verification and retained evidence
+- `red.log`: first focused command exited 1 because OwnedBrowser namespace/API did not exist (compile RED, not an executed assertion RED).
+- `green.log`: first implementation executed 27 cases, 26 passed and one failed because Windows replacement denial was UnauthorizedAccessException rather than IOException. Test corrected to accept both documented filesystem failures; state-preservation assertions retained.
+- `red-parser.log`: executed 31 cases, 29 passed and two duplicate-JSON-field cases failed because parser accepted duplicates. Parser then hardened. These failing constructor assertions also caused fixture cleanup failures since unexpected successful constructors held leases; test process exit released them.
+- `green-final.log`: `dotnet test tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests.csproj -c Release --no-restore --filter FullyQualifiedName~OwnedBrowser`; exit 0, **31 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped**, duration 2 seconds. Includes traversal, canonical IDs, profile separation, URL admission/default deny, workspace/tab ownership, per-workspace/global caps, durable reopen/close/navigation, exclusive lease, disposed guards, corrupt/oversized/missing/duplicate-property state, foreign-root/profile refusal, Keep/Delete, nested junction deletion refusal, invalid inputs and actual denied atomic replacement with unchanged disk/in-memory state.
+- `build.log`: `dotnet build OpenClicky.sln -c Release`; exit 0, **0 warnings, 0 errors**.
+- `git diff --check`: exit 0 before commit.
+- Complete existing Core test suite not run: parent owns integration and native fixture gates. This worker ran only the disposable OwnedBrowser fixtures. A synthetic Windows junction fixture invokes `cmd /c mklink /J` to create its throwaway junction; no browser or desktop application is launched.
+
+## Limits / integration obligations
+This is browser domain foundation, not a completed owned Chromium browser. Parent must connect a WebView2 host after permitted Opus UI direction; pass the exact owned profile directory, disable host objects and web messages, deny permissions/downloads/external launch and intercept redirects, frames and new windows as well as initial navigation. HTTP(S) admission is not a malicious-site/content or network sandbox. It does not replace existing job access snapshots or approval boundaries.
+
+The store holds an exclusive file lease and serializes callers within an instance. Profile deletion requires caller-chosen Keep/Delete and disposal of WebView2 environments first. Keep retains owned data and permits reopening the same owned ID. Delete refuses missing/foreign markers and any recursive reparse point; it never takes an external user-profile path. Metadata removal is committed before physical deletion, so deletion failure can leave an orphan, not a fully transactional rollback. Failed workspace creation persistence can similarly leave an owned empty profile. State replacement uses a same-directory unique temp file, Flush(true), File.Move(overwrite), cleanup; atomic file replacement is not a multi-file or power-loss transaction. No backup recovery is claimed.
+
+Path/marker checks assume application-owned storage with appropriate OS ACLs. They reject observed reparse points, including ancestors and nested deletion entries, but managed check-then-use is not resistant to a hostile same-user concurrent filesystem swap or forged ownership markers. Disk use by Chromium and retained profiles is not quota-managed; metadata/workspace/tab counts and deletion traversal (100,000 entries) are bounded. The host must enforce disk/process lifetime limits. No browser readiness or release claim is made.
