+# Owned Chromium workspace Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** Use Superpowers test-driven-development. This is the assigned Task 3 only.
+
+**Goal:** Persistent, isolated nonvisual workspace/tab policy for a later WebView2 host.
+**Architecture:** A single exclusive store owns a dedicated `OwnedBrowser-v1` child directory beneath a caller-selected storage parent. Profiles are derived from canonical GUID IDs, never supplied or imported. Mutations validate a candidate, atomically persist it, then replace in-memory state.
+**Tech Stack:** .NET 8, System.Text.Json, xUnit; no new dependencies.
+
+## Global constraints
+No UI, Chromium launch, accounts, settings, coordinator, external-browser sessions or CDP server. No traversal/reparse points. Only HTTP/HTTPS/about:blank navigation. Untrusted pages receive no host objects, privileged messages, downloads, permission grants or external launch authority. Single-process exclusive file lease; explicit removal choice; only owned profiles may be deleted. Tests use disposable directories.
+
+## Exact public API (namespace OpenClicky.Core.OwnedBrowser)
+- `enum ProfileRemoval { Keep, Delete }`
+- `record OwnedTab(Guid Id, string Url)`
+- `record OwnedWorkspace(string Id, string Name, IReadOnlyList<OwnedTab> Tabs)`
+- `static class OwnedBrowserPolicy`: `string CanonicalWorkspaceId(string id)`, `string AdmitNavigation(string url)`, `bool AllowsPermission(string permission)`, `bool AllowsHostObjects`, `bool AllowsWebMessages`, `bool AllowsDownloads`, `bool AllowsExternalLaunch`; constants `MaxWorkspaces=16`, `MaxTabsPerWorkspace=32`, `MaxTotalTabs=128`, `MaxStateBytes=1048576`.
+- `sealed class OwnedBrowserStore : IDisposable`: constructor `(string storageParent)`; `IReadOnlyList<OwnedWorkspace> List()`; `OwnedWorkspace CreateWorkspace(string id, string name)`; `string GetProfileDirectory(string workspaceId)`; `OwnedTab OpenTab(string workspaceId, string url)`; `OwnedTab Navigate(string workspaceId, Guid tabId, string url)`; `void CloseTab(string workspaceId, Guid tabId)`; `void RemoveWorkspace(string workspaceId, ProfileRemoval profileRemoval)`; `void Dispose()`.
+- ArgumentException: invalid ID, name, URL or removal choice. InvalidOperationException: cap, duplicate, ownership, foreign directory or concurrent store. InvalidDataException: corrupt/oversized persisted state. IOException/UnauthorizedAccessException: unsafe paths or filesystem failure. ObjectDisposedException after disposal.
+
+## Files and steps
+- [x] Create `tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests/OwnedBrowser/OwnedBrowserTests.cs`: canonical IDs/traversal, dedicated roots, bad URLs, tab ownership, caps, reopen, corruption, exclusive lease, removal choice, link refusal, atomic failure preservation.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests/OpenClicky.Core.Tests.csproj -c Release --filter FullyQualifiedName~OwnedBrowser`; retain RED log and exact exit.
+- [x] Create `apps/windows/OpenClicky.Core/OwnedBrowser/OwnedBrowserPolicy.cs` (IDs/navigation/default-deny policy and immutable records) and `OwnedBrowserStore.cs` (bounded persistence, ownership and lifecycle).
+- [x] Repeat focused test command to GREEN and run Release build. Complete Core tests are deferred to parent integration because this worker is prohibited from native launches and the existing suite contains process/native smoke fixtures. Retain logs/exits in the report. Inspect diff and commit only these paths plus this subplan and `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-28-owned-browser-report.md`.
+
+## Acceptance details
+Validation on load rejects bad version, duplicate identities/tab IDs, malformed URLs, null data and caps. State file reads are bounded. FileStream.Flush(true) and same-directory File.Move overwrite provide atomic replacement, not a multi-file transaction. Existing nonempty foreign roots/profiles and all traversed reparse points are refused. Removal requires the enum with no default; Keep leaves profile data in place. Delete validates ownership markers and recursively checks for links before deletion. Caller must dispose WebView2 environments before removal; no host exists here. Local hostile concurrent filesystem replacement is outside the managed path-check boundary and must be addressed with OS ACLs by integration.
